    {
      "paragraph": "The synthetic process of core-shell structural mathrm 0.9 mathrm 0.1 mathrm O 2 mathrm . - operatorname 0 . Mn . 504 composite cathode materials is schematically described in Fig. 1. In a typical proc",
      "conditions": [
        {
          "condition_id": "C001",
          "temperature": {
            "value": 80,
            "unit": "C"
          }
        }
      ],
      "property_types": [],
      "extracted_info": {}
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "The XRD patterns of pristine mathrm 0.90.1 O 2 and mathrm 0.9 mathrm 0.1 mathrm O 2 mathrm . - mathrm 0.5 mathrm 1.504 composites are presented in Fig. 2. And the corresponding Rietveld refinement plo",
      "property_types": [
        "Crystal_Space_Group"
      ],
      "extracted_info": {
        "Crystal_Space_Group": [
          {
            "value": "R-3m",
            "method": "XRD",
            "source_text": "hexagonal α-NaFeO2 structure with R-3 m space group"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "In order to further investigate the surface chemical state of pristine mathrm 0.90.1 O 2 and mathrm 0.90.1 O 20.51.5 O 4 composites, XPS analysis is performed. As shown in Fig. 3, there are four peaks",
      "property_types": [
        "Element_Valence_State"
      ],
      "extracted_info": {
        "Element_Valence_State": [
          {
            "value": {
              "Ni": "2+,3+",
              "Mn": "2+,3+,4+"
            },
            "unit": "oxidation state",
            "state": "pristine surface",
            "method": "XPS",
            "source_text": "the Ni 2p peak and Ni 2p peak can be deconvoluted into two peaks, which are assigned to Ni2+ and Ni3+ signals ... with increasing the content of the LiNi0.5Mn1.5O4 shell layer, the Ni 2p3/2 peak and Ni 2p1/2 peak gradually shift to the low binding energy, implying more Ni2+ ions are observed at the surface ... the position of Mn 2p1/2 peak shifts from high binding energy of 643.0 eV CS-0.05 to low binding energy of 641.7 eV CS-0.2, indicating the amount of Mn3+ is increased ... The emergent Mn3+ ions mainly originated from the interfacial oxidation of Mn2+ to Mn3+ in LiNi0.9Co0.1O2 core by Mn4+ in LiNi0.5Mn1.5O4 shell"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "The morphology and microstructure of the pristine mathrm 0.90.1 O 2 and core-shell mathrm 0.90.1 O 20.51.5 O 4 composites are further investigated by SEM tests. As depicted in Fig. 4a-d, all the sampl",
      "property_types": [
        "Secondary_Particle_Size_Distribution"
      ],
      "extracted_info": {
        "Secondary_Particle_Size_Distribution": [
          {
            "value": {
              "D50": 12
            },
            "unit": "μm",
            "method": "SEM",
            "source_text": "all the samples are composed of abundant primary particles, which exhibit spherical morphology with a uniform monodisperse distribution Fig. S3a and an average secondary particle size of 12 μm."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "The thermal stability of samples was analyzed with differential scanning calorimeter DSC. The sample was charged to 4.3 V and disassembled in Ar-filled glovebox, and then tested. The DSC data were col",
      "conditions": [
        {
          "condition_id": "C002",
          "temperature": {
            "value": 400,
            "unit": "C"
          },
          "voltage_range": {
            "min": 4.3,
            "max": 4.3,
            "unit": "V",
            "reference": "Li/Li+"
          },
          "electrode_config": "half_cell",
          "test_method": "DSC"
        }
      ],
      "property_types": [],
      "extracted_info": {}
    },
    {
      "paragraph": "mathrm 0.9 mathrm 0.1 mathrm 2 and mathrm 0.90.120.250.753 precursors were mixed with 5 wt.% excess of LiOH⋅H O Aladdin, 99.8%. The mixtures were calcined at 450 circ mathrm C for 6 h and then 740 cir",
      "conditions": [
